<item><title>Uganda ranks 23rd of 56 Commonwealth countries on youth AI readiness</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/ug/uganda-ranks-23rd-of-56-commonwealth-countries-on-youth-ai-40fec2/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/ug/uganda-ranks-23rd-of-56-commonwealth-countries-on-youth-ai-40fec2/</guid><category>Uganda</category><description>A Commonwealth study says Uganda scores 47.0 out of 100, below its readiness benchmark of 53, and that AI could add US$899 million to its GDP over a decade.</description><pubDate>Fri, 13 Nov 2026 07:00:22 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/ug.jpg" length="32020" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/ug.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>UAE reopens visa applications for Ugandans after Ebola curbs</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/ug/uae-reopens-visa-applications-for-ugandans-after-ebola-curbs-7110b5/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/ug/uae-reopens-visa-applications-for-ugandans-after-ebola-curbs-7110b5/</guid><category>Uganda</category><description>Ugandans may apply for UAE visas again, provided they have spent at least 21 days outside Uganda before travelling, the emirate&apos;s authorities announced on Wednesday.</description><pubDate>Thu, 12 Nov 2026 17:18:02 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/ug.jpg" length="32020" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/ug.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
